# What belongs in this repository: sources, the engineering record, and the few
# outputs that cannot be regenerated. Everything a tool rebuilds stays out, so a
# diff shows real design changes and not the noise of the last run.
#
# Tracked on purpose, even though they look like "working files":
#   AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md   the entry point every agent and every new session
#                          reads. Uncommitted, a fresh clone has no context and
#                          the problem they solve comes straight back.
#   docs/                  goal, open issues, decision records. This is the
#                          engineering record of a safety device, not scratch.

# --- Firmware build products -------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in build/ is tracked any more. The .hex images used to be, because
# they were "what Proteus runs" - but a tracked binary goes stale silently, and
# two of these images drive PB3 with OPPOSITE meanings: the eight-channel image
# asserts it to permit running, the legacy single-channel image asserts it on
# over-temperature. Flashing the wrong stale file inverts the safety function
# with no visible symptom (I-031). Build them: firmware/build.ps1.
firmware/build/

# --- KiCad ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# fp-lib-table and sym-lib-table are project configuration and stay tracked.
*.kicad_prl
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*-backups/
_autosave-*
fp-info-cache
*-cache.lib
*-rescue.lib
~*.lck
.history/

# Specctra files handed to and returned by the autorouter.
*.dsn
*.ses

# --- Proteus ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The .pdsprj project is tracked; per-user workspace and auto-backups are not.
**/Project Backups/
*.workspace
*.pdsbak

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- Generated hardware output ------------------------------------------------
# production/ is where a release is assembled. Nothing in it is a source.
production/
# production/ is local. When a revision is actually ORDERED, copy its upload zip
# to hardware/8ch/fabricated/<rev>/ and commit it - the same reason the
# single-channel Gerbers below are tracked: once the sources move on, that zip
# is the only way to know what a board in the field is.
hardware/8ch/output/
hardware/8ch/gerbers/
hardware/8ch/tmp/
hardware/8ch/tmp-*/
# Scratch an agent leaves behind. On 2026-09-07 a delegated run's experiment
# folder and seven half-built sheet files were swept into a commit by
# `git add -A` while that agent was still writing them.
hardware/8ch/route.log
hardware/8ch/*.net
# The netlist-baseline-*.json files are NOT ignored: they are the
# connectivity contract every schematic edit is checked against
# (netlist_fingerprint.py). Only the raw exported *.net above is scratch.
hardware/8ch/BOM.csv
# The two-layer backup variant (I-025) produces the same scratch.
hardware/8ch-2layer/output/
hardware/8ch-2layer/route.log
hardware/8ch-2layer/*.net
hardware/8ch-2layer/BOM.csv

# Check reports. Rewritten on every run; their numbers are quoted in
# docs/STATE.md, which is the thing worth reviewing.
**/drc-report.rpt
**/erc-report.rpt
**/drc-report.txt
**/*-report.rpt

# Renders, layer PDFs and tool analysis dumps. All regenerable, and the
# kicad-happy JSON alone is 1.3 MB of machine output nobody reads.
hardware/**/output/*.png
hardware/**/output/*.pdf
hardware/**/output/*.json
hardware/**/output/*.svg
hardware/**/output/*.step
hardware/**/output/*.wrl
docs/reference/analysis/

# hardware/single-channel/gerbers/ and output/thermocouple_meter_gerbers.zip are
# deliberately NOT ignored: they are the archive of what was actually
# fabricated. Once the sources move on those files cannot be reproduced, and
# they are how a board in the field is identified.

# --- Editors and scratch --------------------------------------------------------
# Konnect's local log folder, created in the repo root on 2026-09-14.
konnect/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.log

# --- Operating system ------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
